  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1154 PM CDT WED OCT 28 2026\n\nAn upper-level ridge continues to weaken across the Southeast as\na shortwave trough lifts over the Northern Plains, yielding west-\nsouthwesterly flow aloft heading into the weekend. Over the next\ncouple of days, Tropical Storm Vance will move inland along the\nwestern coast of Mexico, spreading tropical moisture across\nMexico and into the Plains and Southeast by the weekend.\nConsequently, rain chances return to Central Alabama, with the\nhighest probabilities expected Saturday evening through Sunday\nmorning. Some timing uncertainty remains regarding onset, with a\nlow chance for light rain during Halloween evening festivities.\n\nWeak ridging will bring a return to dry conditions for much of\nnext workweek. Guidance will continue to be monitored for mid-to-\nlate week upper-level troughing, as recent trends suggest\nadditional opportunities for showers and thunderstorms.\n\nOtherwise, light winds and mostly clear skies will favor patchy\nriver fog during the late night and early morning hours over the\nnext few days.\n\n16",
